1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,100
Your reranker raised nDCG by one
point on 1,000 queries.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,300
Is that a real gain?

3
00:00:08,317 --> 00:00:13,917
Say the per-query difference has a
standard deviation of about 0.25.

4
00:00:14,217 --> 00:00:20,717
Divide by the square root of 1,000, and the
standard error is about 0.008.

5
00:00:21,317 --> 00:00:26,942
That makes the 95% interval about
plus or minus 1.6 points.

6
00:00:27,950 --> 00:00:31,150
So a gain of 2-3 points is detectable.

7
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:33,600
A gain of 1 point is not.

8
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,825
Compare per query, with a paired test,
before you call it a win.

9
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:41,475
The full article is on vidyal.ai.
